@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using SpaceSails.Core
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE CONVERGENCE REVEAL, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* #422 — THE CONVERGENCE. The marquee one-time beat: the two rabbit holes (PROJEKTI KAAMOS and NEBULA
       MUTUAL) turn out to be one story — the Expanse moment. Fired by MaybeFireConvergence on the single edge
       BOTH arcs cross their joint threshold; marked seen (persisted) so it never re-plays. Full staged reveal
       card, above everything (a catch that just triggered it sits beneath). The #391 sanity throw is the
       #226 lane's hook (ArcConvergence.ConvergenceSanityShockHook = the heaviest in the game). *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="convergence-backdrop" @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseConvergenceReveal)">
            <OverlayShell class="convergence-card" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="btn btn-light convergence-close" DismissFace="Close"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseConvergenceReveal)">
                @* The stamp is two marks and no words. It used to read "THE THREADS CROSS" over a headline
                   reading "Two mysteries. One truth." — which is the card announcing its own conclusion
                   before the captain has read a line of it. The marks are the two arcs; that is all the
                   card is willing to say in its own voice. *@
                <div class="convergence-stamp">◼ ❄</div>
                @* #528 · THE PLATE. The biggest reveal in the game was a text div while a routine collector
                   shakedown had a painted portrait. It is a PLATE, not an illustration of the lines below
                   it: two filing systems that were always one building, and nobody in the room to react.
                   The alt text describes the PICTURE and not the plot, for the same reason. onerror-hides,
                   so a missing file leaves this card exactly as it was. *@
                <img class="convergence-img" src="@ArcConvergence.ArtFile"
                     alt="Two filing systems, one warm and papered and one cold and steel, meeting at a single shared cabinet."
                     onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
                @* #422 · THE COLLISION (owner ruling 2026-09-17, option B). Two sentences the captain is
                   already carrying, one above the other, UNANNOTATED — no names, no labels, no joining
                   sentence, nothing saying which port they came from or what they add up to. Both are
                   bound to the shard that authored them, so the card can never quote a line the world
                   does not say; ArcConvergence.KaamosSideShard / NebulaSideShard make sure both are in
                   the ledger before this card can open. *@
                <div class="convergence-body">“@KaamosLore.HolderConvergenceLine”</div>
                <div class="convergence-body">“@NebulaLore.AdjusterConvergenceLine”</div>
                @* The closing line is the one thing the card says for itself, and it is not an
                   explanation — it names no fact either voice has not already named. The card used to
                   close on eight sentences of exposition that spent both arcs' capstone reveals. *@
                <div class="convergence-foot">@ArcConvergence.ConvergenceReveal</div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
